#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179451 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/id #uuid "500e1ff1-1a58-57f5-8d85-32ff78dafb35" :question/math-academy-id "e-6117" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[4, 6]$\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 6]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j$, where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nis just the length of the interval $[2, 6]$. So, we have\n\n$$\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j} = 6 - 2 = 4\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i$, we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i} &= (x_{1} + x_{0})Δx_{1} + (x_{2} + x_{1})Δx_{2} + ⋯ + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})Δx_{n} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{0})(x_{1} - x_{0}) + (x_{2} + x_{1})(x_{2} - x_{1}) + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})(x_{m} - x_{m - 1}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&=-x_{0}^{2} + x_{m}^{2} \\\\\n&= x_{m}^{2} - x_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 6^{2} - 4^{2} \\\\\n&= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j = 20\\cdot 4 = 80\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179514 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/id #uuid "e2f01953-2fb1-5ddb-83ae-5d8a73e7f7ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-9482" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1, 2]$\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 3]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n {3} \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j$, where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)3Δx_{i}Δy_{j} &= 3∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δx_{i}Δy_{j} \\\\\n&= 3∑_(i = 1)^(m)Δx_{i}∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nare just the lengths of the intervals $[-1, 2]$ and $[2,3]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)Δx_{i} &= 2 - (-1) = 3, \\\\\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j} &= 3 - 2 = 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 9\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a56efb23-4fb8-51bc-b762-55181a3cb253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177461} {:answer/id #uuid "09973326-24c2-52cb-bec5-3ec0b52b6c90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177462} {:answer/id #uuid "3941c435-42fa-52d2-bf17-be580fd5055e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177463} {:answer/id #uuid "3b076f26-a20f-5937-9362-6f275778ef81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177464} {:answer/id #uuid "3b2efd7e-9334-5697-85e2-5c5353caacf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a56efb23-4fb8-51bc-b762-55181a3cb253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177461} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dfdd3f4-2382-5b16-b34f-62244e473bdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177460}] :question/id #uuid "7cb18f0a-5793-5799-850f-ef66cbf9de18" :question/math-academy-id "q-122867" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0, 2]$\n- $P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[1, 6]$\n\nCalculate $∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δx_{i}Δy_{j}$, where $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$."}]}
